    "summary": {
      "en": "Descendants of the Prophet's uncle al-Abbas, the Abbasids moved the caliphate's centre to Iraq and founded Baghdad. Their early centuries saw a flowering of science and letters; real power later passed to Buyid and Seljuk sultans, and the Mongols ended the Baghdad caliphate in 1258.",
